 The staged consumer fixture retains its worker's exact env-exec lease receipt
 and actual typed retirement/cleanup snapshots in private evidence. Missing
 snapshots stay null; testcase success does not prove lease release or reaping.
+A successful action return and disposal of its persistent worker are separate
+observations. Preserve the lease's original status, exit code and reason when
+the fixture intentionally disposes that worker; do not label it a natural
+worker exit. The source-pinned legacy RCC3 nonreuse test expects `failed`,
+exit code `-1` and reason `child exited non-zero` after an action returns zero.
+That exact version-specific retirement shape is not permission to admit other
+failed receipts. Require the verified artifact/lease and both actual typed
+cleanup snapshots to satisfy their measured wrapper, captured-descendant,
+snapshot and error predicates. These snapshots do not expose independent
+worker reader observations; keep that qualification unavailable rather than
+substituting the outer supervisor's independently measured cleanup.
